From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Dalessio <mike.dalessio@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 15:02:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(CRuby): use-after-free in XPathContext document
 lifetime

XPathContext referenced its document only through the underlying
libxml2 context struct, and never marked the Ruby document for GC, so
the document could be freed by the garbage collector while the
context was still in use. Evaluating an expression on such a context
could then read freed memory.

Add a mark function that keeps the source document reachable for as
long as the XPathContext itself is reachable.

ref: https://github.com/sparklemotion/nokogiri/security/advisories/GHSA-p67v-3w7g-wjg7

Fixes: CVE-2026-57437

[Shivani: backported to nokogiri-1.13.6, adapting the fix to this
version's old-style Data_Wrap_Struct(klass, mark, free, data) API
instead of the rb_data_type_t/TypedData struct used upstream; dropped
test changes]
Signed-off-by: Shivani Agarwal <shivani.agarwal@broadcom.com>
---
 ext/nokogiri/xml_xpath_context.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/nokogiri/xml_xpath_context.c b/ext/nokogiri/xml_xpath_context.c
index c481900..de48ad1 100644
--- a/ext/nokogiri/xml_xpath_context.c
+++ b/ext/nokogiri/xml_xpath_context.c
@@ -17,6 +17,17 @@ deallocate(xmlXPathContextPtr ctx)
   NOKOGIRI_DEBUG_END(ctx);
 }
 
+/* keep the source document alive for as long as this XPathContext is reachable, so that
+ * evaluating an expression can't read freed memory if the document has otherwise become
+ * unreachable. */
+static void
+mark(xmlXPathContextPtr ctx)
+{
+  if (ctx->doc && DOC_RUBY_OBJECT_TEST(ctx->doc)) {
+    rb_gc_mark(DOC_RUBY_OBJECT(ctx->doc));
+  }
+}
+
 /* find a CSS class in an HTML element's `class` attribute */
 static const xmlChar *
 builtin_css_class(const xmlChar *str, const xmlChar *val)
@@ -384,7 +395,7 @@ new (VALUE klass, VALUE nodeobj)
   xmlXPathRegisterFuncNS(ctx, (const xmlChar *)"local-name-is", NOKOGIRI_BUILTIN_URI,
                          xpath_builtin_local_name_is);
 
-  self = Data_Wrap_Struct(klass, 0, deallocate, ctx);
+  self = Data_Wrap_Struct(klass, mark, deallocate, ctx);
   return self;
 }
 
